CPANEL GIT + TANSTACK START DEPLOYMENT

This repository is configured for TanStack Start SPA mode and Apache/cPanel static hosting.

Deployment flow:
GitHub -> cPanel Git Version Control -> .cpanel.yml -> npm install -> npm run build -> dist/client -> public_html

Requirements:
- cPanel Git Version Control must be configured to deploy this repository.
- Your cPanel account must have Node.js/npm available (normally through Application Manager / Setup Node.js App).
- If npm is not available in the deployment environment, cPanel will stop with an explicit error rather than silently deploying a broken site.

After deployment, public_html should contain the TanStack SPA shell (_shell.html), assets/, public assets, and .htaccess.

The old GitHub Actions FTP workflow has been disabled because you are using cPanel Git Version Control. This prevents two deployment systems from competing with each other.

The .htaccess file rewrites application routes to _shell.html while allowing existing files and directories to be served normally.
